+
+## DuckOS Beelzebub AV Event Forwarding
+
+The optional `core.tracings.beelzebub-av` sink forwards a bounded copy of each tracer event to the local DuckOS BAV bridge. It is additive: stdout, RabbitMQ and Beelzebub Cloud keep their existing primary strategy. The forwarder uses a small in-memory queue, short request timeouts and non-blocking enqueue so a stopped BAV receiver cannot stall honeypot protocol workers.
+
+The destination must be an HTTP loopback URL ending in `/v1/events`; remote hosts and redirects are rejected. Configure `auth-token-file` to the bridge's owner-only `ingest.token` file. Use the local Beelzebub process or a container sharing the host network namespace; ordinary Docker bridge networking cannot reach the host loopback listener. The bridge stores normalized hashes and classifications, not the raw credentials, cookies, commands or request bodies.
 
 
 ## Beyond Beelzebub Runtime
